TRACK 1 GATE 0 -- full-knowledge oracle bound (seed 60100, 1488 hands)
  Survey-adopted gate (Richards & Amir IJCAI-07): v5's exact config but
  every sampled world = the opponent's TRUE hidden hand (stock order
  still unknown; _world_weight forced to 1 so the true world is never
  vetoed). Upper-bounds ANY opponent-hand belief improvement in-search.
  oracle-v5 vs v5              +15.91 +/- 1.44    PASS -- huge headroom
  (results/v6_gate0_oracle.log; oracle_gate.py. For scale: v5 vs v4 was
  +1.20. Scrabble precedent realized ~14% of its oracle bound, which
  here would be ~+2.2 pts/hand.)

TRACK 1 -- particle filter offline development (seed 61000 dev streams)
  particle.py: sequential PF, N particles of the opp's hidden hand;
  tau-softmax likelihoods over the belief_teacher scalarization
  (discard energy dw_after + mu*live), softened draw-gain pickup rule,
  optional no-knock evidence; atomic (draw, discard) turns with proper
  importance weights (drew-and-dropped priced at 1/|pool|);
  fully-adapted APF kept-draw step (subsample kdraw, weight by mean
  lik, keep lik-proportional); belief-guided repair on hero-draw
  refutations; ESS<N/2 systematic resampling.
  Dev findings (40-hand teacher streams, scratch sanity runs):
    raw particle marginal Brier LOSES to uniform at N<=512 -- pure
      finite-sample variance (N=4096 recovers to +9.8% but 7.6 s/hand);
    particle posterior DIRECTION beats the calibrated Belief at every
      turn depth (mean mass on truly-held cards, e.g. .49 vs .47 mid,
      .69 vs .65 late) -- the trajectory inference extracts MORE signal;
    the Brier gap is noise, not bias: shrinking the particle marginal
      toward the Belief marginal (lam = n_eff/(n_eff+kappa)) reaches
      +11.9% vs Belief's +12.4% -- a marginal-metric tie.
  NOTE: the searcher consumes SAMPLED WORLDS and world weights, never
  marginals (marginals only feed build_obs plane 5 / BeliefTeacher).
  The offline gate for integration is therefore sampled-world quality
  on the search-consumed statistics (overlap with truth, deadwood
  realism by stage, knock-capability calibration) vs the current
  belief+boost sampler.

  Without rejuvenation the PF only TIED the bel-auto sampler on world
  quality (late overlap .499 vs .509, late dw-gap +15.6 vs +11.9) and
  the floor-clip needed for ensemble survival destroyed the negative
  evidence that makes compositions meldful -- the selectivity-vs-
  diversity tension. RESAMPLE-MOVE (one windowed-MH card-swap per
  particle after each resample; proposal = drop uniform held card, add
  belief-weighted pool card; accepted on the last-6-opp-events
  likelihood, Hastings-corrected) resolves it:

  OFFLINE GATE 1 -- marginal Brier (40-hand dev teacher streams)
    particle (MH, floor .02, kap 80)   +14.6% vs uniform   PASS
    current Belief                     +12.4% vs uniform
  OFFLINE GATE 2 -- sampled-world quality (100 teacher hands, 16/probe)
    late game (opp turns 8+):        overlap  dw-gap  knockBrier
      bel auto (current sampler)      0.508    +11.2    0.459
      particle (MH, floor .02)        0.581     +4.1    0.191   PASS
    mid game (4-7):  particle 0.376/+5.4/0.150 vs auto 0.346/+2.2/0.209
    The late-game deadwood-realism bound that marginals cannot express
    (lesson #9: sampled ~21 vs true ~9) drops to +4.1; knockability
    error -- the statistic that fed v4's +6.59 -- is halved.
  Cost: ~1.8 s/hand at N=256 (incremental, once per hand). In-search
  gate will need a compute-matched control (v4-K80 pattern).

