TRACK 2 -- cross-world exact endgame (endgame.py, built 2026-08-27)
  Survey-corrected design: per-world full-depth max is strategy fusion
  (candidate-asymmetric deferral bias the z-test would CERTIFY -- the
  mechanism of the endgame-v1 negative, lesson #13). Instead: advance
  each world to the hero's next decision, PARTITION worlds by the
  hero-visible observation trace (opp discards/pickups/declines + own
  drawn card), one move per partition (teacher-pruned top-k), recurse
  exact_depth hero decisions, exact full-rules terminal payoffs, per-
  world values flow back so the paired z-test applies unchanged. Root
  candidates stay top-4. Fires only in endgame (stock <= exact_stock)
  on close calls that survive a cheap untruncated screen.
  endgame.py --parity (exact off vs AdaptiveExpert): 143 decisions
  IDENTICAL -- PASS. Smoke: 0.224 s/searched-move under contention.

  BUG FOUND & FIXED (first selection attempt crashed): when the applied
  candidate is the hero's DRAW, the drawn card enters the hand inside
  step_fast BEFORE _advance records observations -- worlds with
  different drawn cards shared one group, breaking the identical-hero-
  hand partition invariant (list.remove crash). Fix: the applied
  action's own observable outcome (the drawn card) prefixes the group
  key. Selection runs with exact_stock=8 (~1 endgame decision/hand --
  power for a low-frequency mechanism).

  SECOND BUG FOUND & FIXED (match-scale crash): sim.restore only
  TRUNCATES move_sheet/game.actions -- content is assumed to be a
  shared prefix. True for v5's same-point sibling worlds; FALSE for
  snapshots on DIVERGED search branches. The engine reads the PHASE
  from the last sheet entries, so restoring a sibling left another
  branch's tail in place and fast_legal_actions surfaced scoring
  actions mid-hand. Fix: _BSnap/_brestore -- branch-safe snapshots
  that also capture and rebuild the sheet/actions tails beyond the
  decision-point base. INFRASTRUCTURE LESSON for all future in-world
  search (incl. tracks 3/4): plain snapshot/restore is only sound for
  rewinding within one line or across content-identical siblings; any
  branching search over diverged states must restore sheet CONTENT,
  not just length.
  Stress: 200 hands (both belief types, 2 seeds, exact_stock=8), 45
  exact escalations, zero crashes, ~5.5 s/hand single-process.

TRACK 2 GATE -- SELECTION (seed 63100, 1488 hands, exact_stock 8)
  exact-eg[d2 k3, pf base] vs v6   -0.17 +/- 1.65    TIE
  Telemetry: 0.64 endgame decisions/hand, 29% escalate to exact
  (~0.19 exact decisions/hand): even +2 pts per exact decision would
  read ~+0.4/hand -- invisible at this CI. Consistent with Long et
  al.'s prediction (gin endgames disambiguate fast; incremental gain
  of exact play over good determinized search is modest) and with
  lesson #13's history (two endgame attempts, two ties).
  VERDICT: mechanism correct (parity + 200-hand stress) but no
  measurable full-match gain; PARKED. To ever resolve it: a
  conditional gate on endgame-reached hands or ~13k hands. The
  reusable assets stand: _BSnap branch-safe snapshots and the
  observation-grouped cross-world evaluator (Track 3's opponent-reply
  branching and Track 4 both need exactly these).
  KEPT INFRASTRUCTURE: endgame.py (ExactEndgameExpert, _BSnap,
  _advance, egmatch with eg-telemetry).

